        </p>
        <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 text-xs font-mono space-y-2 my-4">
          <div class="text-amber-400 font-bold uppercase font-sans">Statutory Accrual Checklist:</div>
          <div>1. 13th and 14th Month Salary Accruals (Mandatory in Philippines, Brazil, Greece).</div>
          <div>2. Untaken Annual Paid Vacation Leave Liquidations.</div>
          <div>3. Mandatory Statutory Notice Pay (typically 1 to 3 months full salary).</div>
          <div>4. Provider Offboarding Processing Administrative Surcharge ($200–$500 per termination).</div>
        </div>
        <p>
          Because the EOR is the statutory employer, they bear legal liability before local labor courts. Consequently, both Deel and Remote will strictly enforce mandatory severance schedules, prohibiting informal handshake settlements.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 6 -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-emerald-400 font-mono">6.</span> Strategic Verdict: When to Choose Deel vs Remote.com
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6">
          <div class="bg-slate-950 border border-emerald-500/30 rounded-xl p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-emerald-400 text-base mb-2">Choose Deel if:</h3>
